{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Held-out validation round 1: restored the full oracle; 28/32 passed. Four failures initially exposed two oracle defects and one implementation gap. Under contract-level correction, case identifiers are treated as a required semantic subset rather than an exact closed set (the implementation's two extra positive controls are valid), and content checks now assert the actual observable input payload rather than note wording/capitalization. The corrected oracle remains RED in 2 nodes for the genuine gap: dataset cases lack explicit applicable/not-applicable metadata, so the applicability matrix is not machine-pinned. Re-dispatching only that missing contract."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786584060452645001,"uuid":"a8e11283-4d7b-4226-b75f-56aee575c3b3"}